For sufficiently small $\rho_{3}>0$, there is an event $\Omega_{n}^{3} \equiv \Omega_{n}^{3}\left(\rho_{3}, \delta\right)$ with $P\left(\Omega_{n}^{3}\right) \rightarrow 1$, as $n \rightarrow \infty$. On this event, for each subset $J$ with $|J|<\rho_{3} n / \log (m)$, for each sign pattern in $\sigma \in \Sigma_{J}$, there is a vector $y\left(\equiv y_{\sigma}\right)$ with


