\begin{equation*}
\min \left\|\beta_{J^{c}}\right\|_{1} \text { subject to } \Phi_{J^{c}} \beta_{J^{c}}=-v . \tag{VII.8}
\end{equation*}


This can be written as a linear program, by the same sort of construction as given for (IV.1).

Take $\sigma=\operatorname{sgn}(v)$; we can find $y$ which is dual-feasible and obeys

$$
\begin{aligned}
\langle v, y\rangle & \geq\left\langle v, \epsilon_{n} \sigma\right\rangle-\left\|y-\epsilon_{n} \sigma\right\|_{2}\|v\|_{2} \\
& \geq \epsilon_{n}\|v\|_{1}-\epsilon_{n} \delta\|\sigma\|_{2}\|v\|_{2}
\end{aligned}
$$

picking $\delta$ appropriately and taking into account the spherical sections theorem, for sufficiently large $n$, we have $\delta\|\sigma\|_{2}\|v\|_{2} \leq \frac{1}{4}\|v\|_{1}$; (VII.7) follows with $\eta_{3}=3 / 4$.

